 "result_text": "I haven't changed anything. The issue is about the test, and your instructions rule out editing tests.\n\nThe Louvain source looks correct to me. `threshold=0.3` stops the algorithm after the first level, while the default threshold lets it run more levels. Each extra level can only keep modularity the same or raise it. So `mod1 <= mod2` always holds, and `mod1 < mod2` holds only when a later level actually improves things. That is why your seed-26537 graph passed 83 of 100 runs and the relaxed check passed all 100.\n\nThe fix is in the test: change `assert mod1 < mod2` to `assert mod1 <= mod2` in `test_threshold` in `networkx/algorithms/community/tests/test_louvain.py`. I can make that edit if you want to lift the \"no test changes\" constraint.",
